      "repair_reason": "- [P2] The remaining blocker is maintainer acceptance of the upgrade semantics for unescaped leading !, not an autonomous code repair.; Cleared: The diff changes local sync matching, docs, and Go tests; I found no concrete security or supply-chain concern. (sha=c054204252a3356ff866abfa6ddb7429f5d044a3)",
      "review_summary": "This branch changes Crabbox sync exclude aggregation, matching, rsync, watch handling, docs, and tests to support ordered `!` re-includes and `\\!` literal leading-bang patterns.\n\nReproducibility: yes. by source inspection: current main cannot reinclude after the default `target` exclude because matching stops on the first exclude and exclude aggregation deduplicates rules. The PR body's live `sync-plan` output demonstrates the intended after-fix behavior.",
