      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: allow crabboxignore reinclude patterns",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Teach `.crabboxignore` matching to honor ordered negation patterns prefixed with `!`.\n- Add coverage for re-including a source directory named `target` while still excluding unrelated build output paths.\n- Preserve repeated rules for last-match-wins semantics, support `\\!` literal paths, and apply the same result to manifests, rsync transfer, and watch mode.\n\n## Why\nCrabbox's default sync excludes include broad names such as `target`. Some repos use `target` as a generated source package path, so they need a precise way to opt that source path back into sync without disabling the default output exclusions globally.\n\n## Validation\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go test -race ./...`\n- `go build -trimpath -o bin/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox`\n- `node scripts/check-command-docs.mjs`\n- Structured autoreview clean on the full branch (0.91)\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBuilt the real CLI, then ran `crabbox sync-plan --limit 20` in a Git repository containing:\n\n- `apps/backend/app/connectors/target/schemas.py` (precisely re-included);\n- `build/target/debug.o` (still excluded by the default `target` rule);\n- `!cache/private.bin` (excluded by the escaped literal `\\!cache` rule).\n\n```text\nsync candidate: 3 files, 75 B\ntop files:\n  44 B       .crabboxignore\n  18 B       apps/backend/app/connectors/target/schemas.py\n  13 B       README.md\ntop dirs:\n  57 B       .\n  18 B       apps/backend\n```\n\nThe re-included source file is present; the unrelated build output and literal leading-bang directory are absent.\n",
        "branch": "agent/crabboxignore-reinclude-20260708",
